From 5266faef220216ac18fe528a0ce2c7e9fe4d1f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: play games in .zip and .7z files

Unpacked into <Wimp$ScrapDir>.PCSXGame a megabyte at a time on null
events (the desktop keeps multitasking), played from there and deleted
when the game is closed or replaced, or PCSX quits. Zip: stored,
deflate, LZMA, zip64 (miniz from the core). 7z: LZMA, LZMA2 and copy
streamed, other methods in small blocks (the LZMA SDK's 7z reader,
public domain, in frontend/riscos/lzma). The library lists archives
with a game in them and reads their serials while idle.
